# ESP-IDF build output + generated config (sdkconfig.defaults is the tracked source).
#
# managed_components/ matters beyond tidiness: ESP-IDF downloads third-party
# components there, and tests/tooling/port_purity_check.sh scans untracked files
# too. Vendored tinyusb carries a Zephyr OSAL header, which the gate correctly
# reads as a Zephyr include inside the ESP tree -- so without this line a plain
# `make esp-build APP=satellite` turns `make check` red for code nobody here
# wrote. examples/esp32/reader ignores the same paths for the same reason.
/build/
/sdkconfig
/sdkconfig.old
/dependencies.lock
/managed_components/
